IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-inspectors`

-- g5-tests-inspectors.l4: tests of g5-inspectors.l4 (ss.30 to 32).
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.30 to 32 (inputs/law.wiki lines 247 to 265) and of Third
-- Schedule item (7) (line 724) BEFORE any of this was run.  Each assertion is one case of the section cited.
-- The #TRACE directives exercise the regulative rules; a DEONTIC cannot be compared, so the expected result is
-- written above each one as `-- EXPECT:` and checked by work/g5/tracecheck.py (reported in FRAGMENT-G5.md).
-- A conforming act ends a trace in FULFILLED; an act the guard does not accept leaves the rule STANDING.

§ `Tests of ss 30 to 32`

§§ `Fixtures`

--                           criminal  disciplinary  indictment  complaint
`no offences on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a criminal conviction on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a disciplinary conviction only on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an indictment pending on record` MEANS `Record of offences` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Candidate: employee, record, opinion that an offence makes him unfit, training, further conditions (NOTHING: none directed)
--                                                                        employee  record                                   opinion  training  further
`an eligible candidate`                 MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE,  `no offences on record`,                 FALSE,   TRUE,     NOTHING
`a candidate who is not an employee`    MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF FALSE, `no offences on record`,                 FALSE,   TRUE,     NOTHING
`a convict the Minister finds unfit`    MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE,  `a criminal conviction on record`,        TRUE,    TRUE,     NOTHING
`a convict the Minister does not find unfit` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE, `a criminal conviction on record`,      FALSE,   TRUE,     NOTHING
`an opinion with no conviction`         MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE,  `no offences on record`,                 TRUE,    TRUE,     NOTHING
`a candidate with a pending indictment` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE,  `an indictment pending on record`,       TRUE,    TRUE,     NOTHING
`a disciplinary convict the Minister finds unfit` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE, `a disciplinary conviction only on record`, TRUE, TRUE, NOTHING
`an untrained candidate`                MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE,  `no offences on record`,                 FALSE,   FALSE,    NOTHING
`a candidate who meets the further conditions` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE, `no offences on record`,              FALSE,   TRUE,     (JUST TRUE)
`a candidate who fails the further conditions` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE, `no offences on record`,              FALSE,   TRUE,     (JUST FALSE)

`all six powers` MEANS
    LIST `require name, address and identification`
       , `require information or a document`
       , `enter a place to supervise`
       , `make measurements and tests`
       , `order measurements and tests kept`
       , `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`

`the first two powers only` MEANS
    LIST `require name, address and identification`
       , `require information or a document`

-- Inspector at work: authorised, powers, acting for supervision, performing function, badge visible, badge identifies,
-- holds certificate, certificate states function and powers, certificate demanded, shown on demand, the Law has commenced for the work
--                                                  authorised  powers                        supervising  performing  badge   identifies  holds   states  demanded  shown
`an inspector who is fully equipped`    MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE,  `all six powers`,            TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector not performing his function` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`,           TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector with no badge in sight`   MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE,  `all six powers`,            TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector whose badge does not identify him` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`,     TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector with no certificate`      MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE,  `all six powers`,            TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector whose certificate does not state his powers` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector whose certificate was demanded and shown` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`, TRUE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,   TRUE, TRUE
`an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,   FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector who showed a certificate nobody demanded` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE, TRUE
`an employee who was never authorised`  MEANS `An inspector at work` OF FALSE, `all six powers`,            TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector with the first two powers` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `the first two powers only`,   TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector not acting for supervision` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`,            FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, `all six powers`, TRUE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE

-- Place: reason limb 1, reason limb 2, dwelling, court order, holder consented
--                                              limb 1  limb 2  dwelling  order  consent
`a workshop where a worker is suspected`  MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a workshop where an engager is suspected` MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a workshop with no suspicion`            MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a dwelling with a court order`           MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a dwelling with the holder's consent`    MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE
`a dwelling with neither`                 MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a dwelling with both`                    MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`a dwelling with consent but no suspicion` MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE

-- Demand: demanded, thing, concerned, secures or eases
--                                                demanded  thing                                              concerned  secures
`a demand for a document`                 MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF TRUE,  `a document that is not computer output`,                                  TRUE,  TRUE
`a demand for computer output`            MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF TRUE,  `computer output as defined in the Computers Law`, TRUE, TRUE
`a demand for mere information`           MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF TRUE,  `information that is not in a document`,        TRUE,  TRUE
`a demand on a person not concerned`      MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF TRUE,  `a document that is not computer output`,                                  FALSE, TRUE
`a demand for a document that serves nothing` MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF TRUE, `a document that is not computer output`,                               TRUE,  FALSE
`a demand never actually made`            MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF FALSE, `a document that is not computer output`,                                  TRUE,  TRUE

§§ `s 30 -- candidates for authorisation`

-- s.30(b)(1) (src:250): not convicted of an offence that in the Minister's opinion makes him unfit.
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `an eligible candidate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `a convict the Minister finds unfit`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `a convict the Minister does not find unfit`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `an opinion with no conviction`
-- A pending indictment is no bar under s.30(b)(1), which has no pending-proceedings limb (contrast s.35(2)).
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `a candidate with a pending indictment`
-- Fork F-OFFENCE: a disciplinary conviction counts only on the alternative reading.
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `a disciplinary convict the Minister finds unfit`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b)(1), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too` `a disciplinary convict the Minister finds unfit`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too` `an eligible candidate`

-- s.30(b)(2) (src:251): suitable training as the Minister directed.
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(2) — the candidate received suitable training, as the Minister directed` `an eligible candidate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b)(2) — the candidate received suitable training, as the Minister directed` `an untrained candidate`

-- s.30(b)(3) (src:252): further conditions as the Minister directed; none directed means none to meet.
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(3) — the candidate meets the further conditions of eligibility the Minister directed` `an eligible candidate`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(3) — the candidate meets the further conditions of eligibility the Minister directed` `a candidate who meets the further conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b)(3) — the candidate meets the further conditions of eligibility the Minister directed` `a candidate who fails the further conditions`

-- s.30(a) with (b) (src:248-252): a Ministry employee, and all of the three.  A person who is not an employee is
-- never answered TRUE, however well he meets (b)(1) to (3).
#ASSERT `s 30(a) — the candidate is an employee of the Ministry` `an eligible candidate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(a) — the candidate is an employee of the Ministry` `a candidate who is not an employee`
#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `an eligible candidate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `a candidate who is not an employee`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `a candidate who is not an employee`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(2) — the candidate received suitable training, as the Minister directed` `a candidate who is not an employee`
#ASSERT `s 30(b)(3) — the candidate meets the further conditions of eligibility the Minister directed` `a candidate who is not an employee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `a convict the Minister finds unfit`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `an untrained candidate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `a candidate who fails the further conditions`
#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `a candidate who meets the further conditions`
#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `a convict the Minister does not find unfit`

-- Acts for the traces.
`the authorisation of an eligible employee` MEANS `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` `an eligible candidate` `all six powers`
`the authorisation of a non-employee` MEANS `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` `a candidate who is not an employee` `all six powers`
`the authorisation of an unfit convict` MEANS `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` `a convict the Minister finds unfit` `all six powers`
`the authorisation of an untrained employee` MEANS `authorise an employee of the Ministry as an inspector` `an untrained candidate` `the first two powers only`

-- s.30(a) (src:248), duty reading: authorising an employee satisfies it; authorising a non-employee does not.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 30(a) — the Minister shall authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of an eligible employee` AT 5
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 30(a) — the Minister shall authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of a non-employee` AT 5
-- No time is stated, so waiting breaches nothing: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 30(a) — the Minister shall authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)
-- Fork F-DUTY: read as a power, the same act is FULFILLED; with no time stated the permission is never spent, so
-- doing nothing leaves it standing (it is not a breach, which is the difference from the duty reading's meaning).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 30(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of an eligible employee` AT 5
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 30(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise inspectors from among the employees of the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

-- s.30(a), (b) (src:248-252), prohibition: a person who is not an employee, or who fails a limb of (b), must not be authorised.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 30(b) — the Minister shall authorise as an inspector only a person who satisfies all three conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of a non-employee` AT 5
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 30(b) — the Minister shall authorise as an inspector only a person who satisfies all three conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of an unfit convict` AT 5
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 30(b) — the Minister shall authorise as an inspector only a person who satisfies all three conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of an untrained employee` AT 5
-- An eligible person's authorisation is not what the prohibition catches.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 30(b) — the Minister shall authorise as an inspector only a person who satisfies all three conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the authorisation of an eligible employee` AT 5

-- s.30(c) (src:253): notice shall be published.  Inferred actor: the Minister; the other inference is callable.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 30(c) — the Minister shall have notice of an inspector's authorisation published in Reshumot` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `publish notice of an inspector's authorisation in Reshumot` AT 5
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 30(c) — the Minister shall have notice of an inspector's authorisation published in Reshumot` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 30(c) — notice of an inspector's authorisation shall be published in Reshumot by` `the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `publish notice of an inspector's authorisation in Reshumot` AT 5

§§ `s 31 -- the inspector holds and may use a power`

-- s.31 lead-in with s.30(a): authorised, the power conferred, acting to supervise the Law (src:255-256).
#ASSERT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `enter a place to supervise`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an employee who was never authorised` `enter a place to supervise`
#ASSERT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `require name, address and identification`
#ASSERT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `require information or a document`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `enter a place to supervise`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `make measurements and tests`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `order measurements and tests kept`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector not acting for supervision` `enter a place to supervise`

-- Every one of the six powers is usable by the fully equipped inspector (s.31(1) to (4)).
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `require name, address and identification`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `require information or a document`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `enter a place to supervise`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `make measurements and tests`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `order measurements and tests kept`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`

-- A power not conferred is not usable even when s.32 is met.
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `enter a place to supervise`
#ASSERT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector with the first two powers` `require information or a document`

§§ `s 32 -- identification`

-- s.32 lead-in and (1), (2) (src:263-265): on duty, badge visibly worn and identifying, certificate held and stating.
#ASSERT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector who is fully equipped`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector not performing his function`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector with no badge in sight`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector whose badge does not identify him`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector with no certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector whose certificate does not state his powers`
#ASSERT `s 32(1) — the inspector visibly wears a badge identifying him and his function` `an inspector who is fully equipped`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32(1) — the inspector visibly wears a badge identifying him and his function` `an inspector with no badge in sight`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32(1) — the inspector visibly wears a badge identifying him and his function` `an inspector whose badge does not identify him`
#ASSERT `s 32(2) — the inspector holds a certificate signed by the Minister stating his function and powers` `an inspector who is fully equipped`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32(2) — the inspector holds a certificate signed by the Minister stating his function and powers` `an inspector with no certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32(2) — the inspector holds a certificate signed by the Minister stating his function and powers` `an inspector whose certificate does not state his powers`

-- "Both" are required (cumulative): badge without certificate and certificate without badge each fail.
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector with no certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector with no badge in sight`

-- Fork F-DEMAND, the certificate "shown on demand": reading B (taken) makes a refusal to show it, when asked,
-- a failure of limb (2); reading A does not.
#ASSERT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and shown`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown`
#ASSERT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector who showed a certificate nobody demanded`
#ASSERT `s 32, reading A — the inspector may use the powers, showing the certificate on demand being a separate duty` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown`
#ASSERT `s 32, reading A — the inspector may use the powers, showing the certificate on demand being a separate duty` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and shown`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32, reading A — the inspector may use the powers, showing the certificate on demand being a separate duty` `an inspector with no certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 32, reading A — the inspector may use the powers, showing the certificate on demand being a separate duty` `an inspector not performing his function`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` `enter a place to supervise`

-- s.32 as a prohibition (SHANT): using any power without the conditions is a breach by the inspector.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `an inspector`
#TRACE `s 32 — an inspector shall not use the powers unless he is performing his function, wears the badge and holds the certificate` `an inspector with no badge in sight` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `make measurements and tests` AT 3
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `an inspector`
#TRACE `s 32 — an inspector shall not use the powers unless he is performing his function, wears the badge and holds the certificate` `an inspector with no certificate` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 3
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `an inspector`
#TRACE `s 32 — an inspector shall not use the powers unless he is performing his function, wears the badge and holds the certificate` `an inspector not performing his function` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require information or a document` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 32 — an inspector shall not use the powers unless he is performing his function, wears the badge and holds the certificate` `an inspector who is fully equipped` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 3

-- The duty to show the certificate on demand.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 32(2) — an inspector whose certificate is demanded shall show it` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and shown` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `show the certificate signed by the Minister` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 32(2) — an inspector whose certificate is demanded shall show it` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 50)
-- No demand, no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 32(2) — an inspector whose certificate is demanded shall show it` `an inspector who is fully equipped` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 50)

§§ `s 31(1) to (4) -- the powers as MAY rules`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(1) — an inspector may require any person to give his name and address and to show identification` `an inspector who is fully equipped` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require name, address and identification` AT 2
-- With the badge missing the guard refuses the act: the permission stays standing, unexercised.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(1) — an inspector may require any person to give his name and address and to show identification` `an inspector with no badge in sight` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require name, address and identification` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may make measurements and tests` `an inspector who is fully equipped` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `make measurements and tests` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may make measurements and tests` `an inspector with the first two powers` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `make measurements and tests` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may order measurements and tests kept for a period he directs` `an inspector who is fully equipped` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `order measurements and tests kept` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may deal with measurements and tests in another way` `an inspector who is fully equipped` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise` AT 2

§§ `s 31(2) -- demands for information or a document (IP10)`

-- The demand is one the inspector may make (src:258).
#ASSERT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for mere information`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand on a person not concerned`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document that serves nothing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `an inspector with the first two powers` `a demand on a person not concerned`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2) — the demand is one the inspector may make` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a demand for a document`

-- "Document" includes computer output; information that is not in a document is not a document.
#ASSERT `s 31(2) — the thing is a document, which includes computer output` `a document that is not computer output`
#ASSERT `s 31(2) — the thing is a document, which includes computer output` `computer output as defined in the Computers Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2) — the thing is a document, which includes computer output` `information that is not in a document`

-- What G6 consumes for Third Schedule item (7): a document demanded under s.31(2).
#ASSERT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for computer output`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for mere information`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand on a person not concerned`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document that serves nothing`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand never actually made`
-- Fork F-ITEM7: a demand by an inspector who fails s.32 is not "given under s.31(2)" on the reading taken ...
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector with no certificate` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector not performing his function` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an employee who was never authorised` `a demand for a document`
-- ... and is one on the alternative reading, which ignores s.32 but keeps the authorisation and the power.
#ASSERT `s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT `s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` `an inspector with no certificate` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT `s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` `an employee who was never authorised` `a demand for a document`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for mere information`
#ASSERT `s 31(2), s 32 ignored — a document was demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(2) — an inspector may require a person concerned to give information or a document` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require information or a document` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(2) — an inspector may require a person concerned to give information or a document` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand on a person not concerned` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require information or a document` AT 2

§§ `s 31(3) -- entry (trap T30)`

-- s.31(3) (src:259): reason to suppose (either limb); the proviso for a dwelling: court order or consent.
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` `a workshop where a worker is suspected`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` `a workshop where an engager is suspected`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` `a workshop with no suspicion`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` `a workshop with no suspicion`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` `a dwelling with a court order`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` `a dwelling with the holder's consent`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` `a dwelling with both`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) proviso — the place may be entered: it is not a dwelling, or a court order permits it, or the holder consented` `a dwelling with neither`

-- Entry as a whole.  A place that is not a dwelling needs no order and no consent (T30).
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a workshop where a worker is suspected`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a workshop where an engager is suspected`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a workshop with no suspicion`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling with a court order`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling with the holder's consent`
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling with both`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling with neither`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling with consent but no suspicion`
-- The inspector must also hold the power and meet s.32.
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector with the first two powers` `a workshop where a worker is suspected`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a workshop where a worker is suspected`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector with no certificate` `a dwelling with a court order`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an employee who was never authorised` `a workshop where a worker is suspected`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(3) — an inspector may enter a place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a workshop where a worker is suspected` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(3) — an inspector may enter a place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling with neither` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `an inspector`
#TRACE `s 31(3) proviso — an inspector shall not enter a dwelling without a court order or the holder's consent` `a dwelling with neither` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(3) proviso — an inspector shall not enter a dwelling without a court order or the holder's consent` `a dwelling with a court order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(3) proviso — an inspector shall not enter a dwelling without a court order or the holder's consent` `a workshop with no suspicion` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2

§§ `s 31(4) -- the period for keeping measurements and tests (P22)`

-- s.31(4) (src:260).  Direction given on 2026-01-01, a Thursday.  30 days from it end on 2026-01-31 (s.10(a): the
-- day of the direction is not counted).
`a direction of 30 days` MEANS `a number of days directed for keeping` 30
`a direction of 1 month` MEANS `a number of months directed for keeping` 1
`a direction of 1 year` MEANS `a number of years directed for keeping` 1
`a direction to keep until 15 March 2026` MEANS `a last day directed for keeping` (YMD 2026 3 15)

#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction of 30 days` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- Both edges: the last day is inside, the day after is outside; the day of the direction is inside, the day before is outside.
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
-- A month from the 31st ends on the last day of the shorter month (s.10(b)); a year from 29 February ends on 28 February.
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `a direction of 1 month` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2024 2 29) `a direction of 1 year` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction to keep until 15 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction to keep until 15 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 3 16) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction to keep until 15 March 2026`

-- Fork F-P22 (kind V, s.10(c) not applied): a nominal last day that is a rest day stays the last day.  The
-- alternative, with s.10(c), moves it to the next day that is not a rest day.
`a calendar with Saturday 31 January 2026 a rest day` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 1 31)
`a calendar with 31 January and 1 February 2026 rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 1 31, YMD 2026 2 1)
`a calendar with no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction of 30 days` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 31(4), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction of 30 days` `a calendar with Saturday 31 January 2026 a rest day` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `s 31(4), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction of 30 days` `a calendar with 31 January and 1 February 2026 rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 2
#ASSERT `s 31(4), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction of 30 days` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- A stated last day is a date, not a counted period: s.10(c) does not move it.
#ASSERT `s 31(4), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction to keep until 15 March 2026` `a calendar with no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
-- A month from 2025-01-31 ends 2025-02-28 (Friday); with 28 February and 1 March rest days it moves to Sunday 2 March.
`a calendar with 28 February and 1 March 2025 rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2025 2 28, YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 31(4), s 10(c) applied — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `a direction of 1 month` `a calendar with 28 February and 1 March 2025 rest days` EQUALS YMD 2025 3 2
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `a direction of 1 month` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

-- Fork F-START: on the alternative, keeping begins the day AFTER the direction (the direction day is outside, the
-- day after it is inside, the last day is inside and the day after that outside).
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(4), beginning the day after the direction — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
#ASSERT `s 31(4), beginning the day after the direction — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 1 2) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
#ASSERT `s 31(4), beginning the day after the direction — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(4), beginning the day after the direction — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`

§§ `Each power on its own: an inspector who holds just that power, and one who holds every power but that one`

GIVEN p IS A `Power of supervision under section 31`
GIVETH AN `An inspector at work`
`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` p MEANS
    `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (LIST p), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

GIVEN p IS A `Power of supervision under section 31`
GIVETH AN `An inspector at work`
`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` p MEANS
    `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (filter (GIVEN q YIELD NOT (q EQUALS p)) `all six powers`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- A guard that checked some other power than the one the rule is about would pass every one of these.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(1) — an inspector may require any person to give his name and address and to show identification` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` `require name, address and identification`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require name, address and identification` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(1) — an inspector may require any person to give his name and address and to show identification` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` `require name, address and identification`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require name, address and identification` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(2) — an inspector may require a person concerned to give information or a document` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` `require information or a document`) `a demand for a document` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require information or a document` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(2) — an inspector may require a person concerned to give information or a document` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` `require information or a document`) `a demand for a document` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require information or a document` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(3) — an inspector may enter a place` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` `enter a place to supervise`) `a workshop where a worker is suspected` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(3) — an inspector may enter a place` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` `enter a place to supervise`) `a workshop where a worker is suspected` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `enter a place to supervise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may make measurements and tests` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` `make measurements and tests`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `make measurements and tests` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may make measurements and tests` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` `make measurements and tests`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `make measurements and tests` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may order measurements and tests kept for a period he directs` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` `order measurements and tests kept`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `order measurements and tests kept` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may order measurements and tests kept for a period he directs` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` `order measurements and tests kept`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `order measurements and tests kept` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may deal with measurements and tests in another way` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds only the power` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(4) — an inspector may deal with measurements and tests in another way` (`an inspector who is equipped and holds every power but` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `deal with measurements and tests otherwise` AT 2

§§ `s 31(2) and Third Schedule item (7) -- the duty to comply and the violation (IP9, IP10)`

-- The duty to give what was lawfully demanded (implied by item (7)): arises only on a lawful demand.
`give what the inspector demanded, as an act` MEANS `give what the inspector demanded`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `give what the inspector demanded, as an act` AT 9
-- No time is stated for compliance, so waiting breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)
-- A demand by an inspector without his badge is not one he could lawfully make: no duty arises.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a demand for a document` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)
-- A demand on a person not concerned: no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand on a person not concerned` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)
-- A demand never made: no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand never actually made` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)
-- A demand for information alone is lawful and binds, though item (7) prices only a document.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(2) — a person concerned shall give the information or document an inspector lawfully demanded` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for mere information` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)

`the person who did not give the document` MEANS `Person` OF "ID-0042", `an individual`
`the violation of item (7) on 1 March 2026` MEANS
    `Violation` OF `the person who did not give the document`, `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`, "act-0042", (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the violation of item (7) on 1 March 2026`
#ASSERT `the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for computer output` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST `the violation of item (7) on 1 March 2026`
-- The document was given: no violation.
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for a document` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE)
-- Information, not a document: item (7) does not reach it.
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand for mere information` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE)
-- Fork F-ITEM7: the demand was not lawfully made (no badge, certificate refused, never authorised, not concerned): no violation.
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a demand for a document` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` `a demand for a document` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an employee who was never authorised` `a demand for a document` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand on a person not concerned` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT isJust (`the violation committed under s.31(2), if any` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a demand never actually made` `the person who did not give the document` "act-0042" (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE)

§§ `s 63(a) and IP2 -- the powers are used only where the Law has commenced for the work`

-- Authorising inspectors (s.30) is not tied to commencement; using the powers is.  Commencement is an input (G7).
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector holds the power` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` `enter a place to supervise`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` `require information or a document`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` `a workshop where a worker is suspected`
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` `a demand for a document`
-- s.32 alone does not depend on it: the badge, the certificate and being on duty are met.
#ASSERT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work`
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 31(1) — an inspector may require any person to give his name and address and to show identification` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an inspector` DOES `use a power of supervision` `require name, address and identification` AT 2
